If `vgic_allocate_private_irqs_locked()` fails, the code immediately jumps to `out_unlock` without having initialized `kvm->arch.vgic.vgic_dist_base`, `kvm->arch.vgic.rd_regions`, or the VGIC model ID registers. Later, during teardown (e.g., via `kvm_vgic_dist_destroy()`), these uninitialized structures (especially the list head) are accessed, causing a crash or undefined behavior.

