 		kvm_for_each_vcpu(i, vcpu, kvm) {
 			struct vgic_cpu *vgic_cpu = &vcpu->arch.vgic_cpu;
 			kfree(vgic_cpu->private_irqs);
 			vgic_cpu->private_irqs = NULL;
 		}

+		kvm->arch.vgic.vgic_model = 0;
 		goto out_unlock;
 	}
```
Reason:
All static initialization (dist/redist base, list head, and system registers) is moved before the loop that allocates private IRQs. This ensures that even if the allocation fails and we exit early, the distributor and redistributor structures are properly initialized. Additionally, resetting `vgic_model` to 0 on failure prevents the teardown code from using a stale model type (e.g., one that refers to an uninitialized redistributor list).

